<description>&lt;p&gt;The rebuilt flood-damaged town is being promoted as a showcase for the Libyan strongman’s rule while Fezzan revolutionaries continue to contest Haftar’s control in the south. The House of Representatives condemned Zintan’s obstruction of a parliamentary session and the armed closure of Zintan Airport, and the UN special representative welcomed amendments raising the recruitment age to 18, alongside new laws criminalising the conscription of minors. Egypt is balancing its ties with Libya amid eastern Mediterranean tensions. Libya retains Africa’s largest oil reserves but Western majors are not investing. Combat intensity remains low, with 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXkFVX3lxTE1LNWtaVkVtaWR5blozTVduaVhRQXp2UEJhakxwMHhERGpxN2dxSmJzWnpRVktBWHllUWRGb1VacnZlTDFidGxCamNCUWNlQVdTZFpRRnVPM181aEE5TXc?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikAFBVV95cUxOZDJQV3R3Vi1qa0VjYUtBS1RnQUNhWTY4VDlHUTE5a1o5bUZHTzVZMnZwNkt0d2x4MGJhYXZGUmwxNUNLUEkzQlBwOGxENWcxZ1U1UFNVeU12ZkowSjJVZ2hNdW9tUWVNOF9kQ2lFMTROM0lDY19qV1lnMUVwa19lSzJhQnMwWU84NmVBWGVGekM?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Arab Weekly&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirwFBVV95cUxPRXRYU09NQjhUamNjTUxaY0VKcXo3am1MWldRYzRQc000d0JHQ3l6WGdOcElwaF9ScGpPeWQwd0d0VWRLSnRKRGhSTW5pQko0V2gzaUZpT2NxLTlMR09reWlMWGphR1pXdURBVW5WNENNMUJpc3ZrVG9WYjJrbkdWcGVISThWU1cxcGxTQzF4OE1FNV9FTnJsTS0tbXVqU09fenhHMlZ3bWZER2pobEo0?oc=5&quot;&gt;Jurist.org&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwAFBVV95cUxNeTBlZTcyU0RTdFlFdVRjOW1xd1I4aUZQNHlnbGRWeWphVVlhQnZWNWhScDZvaWJJQ3o3U2VjUWxUV055bHp6Nnl3RkVDOFVNNzFmcU9ua1NidVlEZ1BvTVU4TUVLMUVWNW5LZnNZbTNkRUdVTEpENU5CdjI2V25vTnFhZW9tM0o5RFRQZm92eHBNOVFRYTgtV1VNYzU5dl96aFpDeENCUjRkbmJjSnlHQ2lh